==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|erthely}}, {{m|enm|erthlich}}, {{m|enm|ierðlich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eorþlīċ}}, corresponding to {{suffix|en|earth|ly}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|jarðligr|t=earthly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈəːθli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-earthly.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|earthlier}}

# Relating to the [[earth]] or this world, as opposed to heaven; [[terrestrial]].
#: '''''earthly''' joys''
#* {{rfdate||and other bibliographic particulars, eg, title of work, page, url}} {{w|John Milton}}
#*: This '''earthly''' load / Of death, called life.
#* {{rfdate|}} Bible, Phil. iii. 19
#*: whose glory is in their shame, who mind '''earthly''' things
# {{lb|en|negative|informal}} {{non-gloss definition|Used for emphasis}}
#* {{rfdate||and other bibliographic particulars}} {{w|Alexander Pope}}
#*: What '''earthly''' benefit can be the result?
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Made of earth; [[earthy]].
#: {{rfquotek|lang=en|Holland}}

